[moved to stan-dev]

I say again that we really need to fix this message.  Users
continue to freak out about it.

I'm in favor of just eliminating it until someone has
the time and energy to add something more sophisticated,
either something that counts number of problems and reports
if there are too many or offers some kind of logging level to
turn it off or on.

I suppose we could just turn it off during warmup, too,
which is where almost all of the warnings that can be ignored
will occur.

- Bob

On May 7, 2014, at 5:02 PM, Michael Betancourt <betan...@gmail.com> wrote:

> The relevant ratio is not messages / per chain but message / iteration.  If every
> transition of the Markov chain rejects because of this problem you have a bad
> model, if only a few transitions are rejected because of it then you’re okay.
