On Wednesday, May 21, 2014 12:16:38 PM UTC-4, Michael Betancourt wrote:
> Before worrying about the adaptation we have to worry about the well-posedness
> of all of these models.  They need to be reparameterized and checked for heavy
> tails (a la the HMC for hierarchical models paper).  Once we know they fit then
> we can see if the adaptation is still causing problems.

I've been saying for a while that the BUGS models are only useful for demonstrating features of the language. But the slowness or inability to get close to the target acceptance rate holds just as much for the non-BUGS models where we are just sampling from a distribution (e.g. inv_wishart) or are generating the data and fitting the model (everything below funnel_reparam in that matrix). And I think funnel_reparam is a model where the chains ostensibly should converge quickly to the target and they don't with 10000 iterations

funnel_reparam: 0.9700  0.9718  0.9322  0.9772

Ben

