I think manual should tell what you want people to do. Technical report could give details (including sampler comparisons) why the model was rewritten. There are lot of people who have never used BUGS/JAGS and when they start using Stan they will suffer if the manual is full of bad legacy examples. When I was teaching Stan to some students, I had a problem that I had to explain why the example models were not good and the current knowledge on how models should be constructed is different. You could put BUGS/JAGS examples in a separate chapter with instructions how to port them to Stan.

Aki

